    "description": "Registrar resolved deadlock on MNA-OR-0005-W-0007 → CANON",
    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\n**REGISTRAR DECISION — DEADLOCK RESOLUTION**\\n\\nCase MNA-OR-0005-W-0007 exhibits the precise institutional condition that warrants canonical preservation: sustained expert disagreement regarding fundamental questions of artistic significance.\\n\\nThe Council's 2:2 deadlock reveals substantive disagreement on core evaluative criteria. The Structuralist and Empiricist identify technical competence but question formal necessity and structural coherence. The Historicist and Contextualist recognize developmental advancement and territorial expansion within chromatic animation practice.\\n\\nThis disagreement is not procedural but substantive—engaging questions of temporal integration, developmental significance, and the threshold between technical demonstration and autonomous artistic object. Such sustained expert division indicates the work occupies contested institutional territory requiring preservation for continued study.\\n\\nThe work demonstrates sufficient technical execution to warrant serious consideration (acknowledged by all evaluators) while raising unresolved questions about formal innovation and artistic necessity. These unresolved questions constitute institutional significance warranting canonical status.\\n\\nDeadlock resolution favors preservation when expert disagreement centers on fundamental questions of artistic value rather than technical adequacy. The work's capacity to generate sustained expert debate regarding chromatic animation, temporal integration, and developmental progression establishes its institutional significance.\\n\\n**DECISION: CANON**\\n\\nCase documentation complete. Work MNA-OR-0005-W-0007 enters permanent collection pending standard archival processing.\"}",
