    "description": "Registrar resolved deadlock on MNA-OR-0004-W-0012 → CANON",
    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\nThis deadlock itself demonstrates the work's institutional significance. The sustained disagreement between evaluators reveals that MNA-OR-0004-W-0012 operates at a threshold of canonical ambiguity that merits preservation for future institutional analysis.\\n\\nThe split follows predictable evaluative lines: structural and empirical concerns about technical coherence versus historical and contextual recognition of developmental significance and conceptual territory. This pattern indicates the work engages fundamental questions about the boundaries of our collection criteria rather than representing a clear failure or success.\\n\\nThe work's fragmentation of the phrase \\\"words that never\\\" into dispersing elements creates a meta-commentary on incomplete meaning that mirrors the incomplete consensus it has generated. This recursive relationship between form and institutional reception suggests the piece functions as more than its component parts.\\n\\nProcedurally, when sustained expert disagreement occurs over a work that demonstrates technical competence and conceptual coherence, preservation serves the institution's long-term evaluative capacity. Future scholarship may resolve what current evaluation cannot.\\n\\nThe deadlock resolution favors inclusion when the work demonstrates sufficient complexity to generate legitimate interpretive disagreement among qualified evaluators. MNA-OR-0004-W-0012 meets this threshold.\\n\\nCase closed. Work enters permanent collection pending standard archival processing.\"}",
